      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a24e80e-7bbd-4346-b0bf-49a319f69b34"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the family of circles around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in the band ",
 StyleBox["r \[LessEqual] d(c, v) \[LessEqual] s", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"752572c0-04fd-4bc8-bfea-7734e7768c14"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 StyleBox["W = {v : r \[LessEqual] d(c, v) \[LessEqual] s}", "TI"],
 ". A circle of ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " among those whose removal cuts ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " off from every vertex beyond ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 ". When nothing lies beyond ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " the condition is empty."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"77b13609-0b5a-47de-9fd4-2fbee5eea8c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A circle need not exist. On a bipartite graph, such as the square grid, no \
two vertices of one shell are adjacent, so a single shell carries no circle. \
On the square grid the band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + 1} does. On the mesh a single shell usually carries one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b9858153-c740-497d-b6b3-71f71dea2444"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A circle need not be unique. On the square grid, away from the rim, the \
band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + 1} carries one circle and the band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + 2} carries ",
 StyleBox["16\:02b3\:207b\.b9", "TI"],
 ", all of length ",
 StyleBox["8r", "TI"],
 ": the circle of the \[ScriptL]\.b9 norm."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"73342d84-d164-42e9-9701-f9b90edef421"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7b3e7891-90c9-4cc6-8f97-60999940d4b4"],
 " is a symbolic object: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "74b5831b-02a7-4732-970e-3173c9b022b6"],
 " evaluates it on a graph and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ee93451-fc2e-4f99-a302-1a4a00eae0d1"],
 " draws members. A member is a cyclic vertex list; its first vertex is not \
repeated, and its length is its number of vertices."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"51c850dd-2844-4abb-a468-4d863b3fc073"],

